<title>UK: EU grants free-market grains at weekly tender.</title>
<headline>EU grants free-market grains at weekly tender.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-07-31</dateline>
<text>
<p>The European Union on Thursday granted the following licences to export free market grain to non-EU countries at its weekly export tender, the UK's Home Grown Cereals Authority said.</p>
<p>		  Tonnage	  Maximum rebate/tax</p>
<p>Wheat	   170,000	   0.50  Ecu/tonne tax</p>
<p>Barley	   80,000	  11.99  Ecu/tonne rebate</p>
<p>Rye		 1,100	  22.98  Ecu/tonne rebate</p>
<p>--Christopher Lyddon, London newsroom +44 171 542 7928</p>
